**A successful `@claude review` retry never clears `pr/ci-failing`**

```js
const runs = (
  await github.paginate(github.rest.checks.listForRef, {
    owner, repo, ref: pr.head.sha, per_page: 100,
  })
).filter((c) => c.name !== context.job);
// The review poster also reports a commit status, which a retry on main updates.
...
if (runs.some((c) => bad.has(c.conclusion)) || ["failure", "error"].includes(combined.state)) {
```

When the `pull_request`-triggered review dies on the sandbox error, its `claude-review` job leaves a failed check run on the head SHA. The `@claude review` retry runs on `issue_comment`, so its check runs attach to main's SHA. The poster does flip the `claude-review` commit status on the head to `success` (`post-review.script.ts` `setCommitStatus`). But the failed check run on the head is never superseded, and line 103 ORs the two signals, so `runs.some(bad)` keeps returning `pr/ci-failing`.

The PR body accepts that this check fails often, and the retry the tooling recommends (`review-body.utils.ts:123`) is the path that leaves the label stuck. Only a UI re-run or a new push clears it.

One fix: for a check run whose name matches a commit-status context (`claude-review`), let the status decide.

https://github.com/AlexisBalayre/pupitre/blob/acf6c3105eb35202d6f4deca1189e700391ab417/.github/workflows/pr-status.yml#L91-L104

**PRs with no commit status can never reach `pr/ready`**

```js
if (runs.some((c) => c.status !== "completed") || combined.state === "pending") {
  return "pr/ci-pending";
}
```

GitHub's docs for `GET /repos/{owner}/{repo}/commits/{ref}/status` say the combined state is `pending` "if there are no statuses or a context is pending". Only the review preflight (`markNotReviewed`) and the poster write a status. Both run inside the `claude-review` job, whose `if:` requires `github.actor == github.repository_owner`.

So a head that was opened or pushed by Dependabot, a collaborator, or a fork author never gets a status. It reads as pending forever and never reaches `pr/ready`. Commit ff48c71 introduced this when it added the combined-status read.

Checking the individual statuses avoids the empty case. Optionally, also pass `per_page: 100` to `getCombinedStatusForRef`: the `statuses` array is paginated at 30 by default.

https://github.com/AlexisBalayre/pupitre/blob/acf6c3105eb35202d6f4deca1189e700391ab417/.github/workflows/pr-status.yml#L106
